########## US5-4 / FR-027: limite de 10 peticiones por usuario y minuto
# user ya gasto 5 en este minuto (US1-1, US1-7, recommendations, HEAD y US1-3): las 5 siguientes se atienden.

### US5-4 peticion 6 de 10 — expects 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/lists/hu12-vacia/recommendations
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### US5-4 peticion 7 de 10 — expects 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/lists/hu12-vacia/recommendations
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### US5-4 peticion 8 de 10 — expects 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/lists/hu12-vacia/recommendations
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### US5-4 peticion 9 de 10 — expects 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/lists/hu12-vacia/recommendations
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### US5-4 peticion 10 de 10 — expects 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/lists/hu12-vacia/recommendations
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### US5-4 / FR-005, FR-027: la undecima — expects 429 RECOMMENDATION_ERROR_001 con Retry-After
GET {{baseUrl}}/lists/hu12-vacia/recommendations
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

> {%
client.test("status 429", () => client.assert(response.status === 429));
client.test("code", () => client.assert(response.body.code === "RECOMMENDATION_ERROR_001"));
client.test("retry after", () => client.assert(Number(response.headers.valueOf("Retry-After")) >= 1));
%}

### US5-6: otro usuario no se ve afectado — expects 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/lists/hu12-vacia/recommendations
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

> {%
client.test("status 200", () => client.assert(response.status === 200));
%}

########## Parte B: IA activada

### US2-1 / FR-001 a FR-004, FR-011: sugerencias del modelo — expects 200 IA
GET {{baseUrl}}/lists/hu12-canciones/recommendations
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

> {%
client.test("status 200", () => client.assert(response.status === 200));
client.test("from the model", () => client.assert(response.body.origen === "IA"
  && response.body.versionPrompt === "v1"));
client.test("1 to 5, unverified", () => client.assert(response.body.recomendaciones.length >= 1
  && response.body.recomendaciones.length <= 5
  && response.body.recomendaciones.every(r => r.idCatalogo === "" && r.motivo.length <= 120)));
client.global.set("firstAnswer", JSON.stringify(response.body));
%}

### US5-1 / FR-026: la misma lista otra vez, desde la cache — expects 200 con la misma respuesta
GET {{baseUrl}}/lists/hu12-canciones/recommendations
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

> {%
client.test("status 200", () => client.assert(response.status === 200));
client.test("same answer", () => client.assert(
  JSON.stringify(response.body) === client.global.get("firstAnswer")));
%}

### US5-2: borrar la lista — expects 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/lists/hu12-canciones
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### US5-2: crearla de nuevo con otras canciones — expects 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/lists
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nombre": "hu12-canciones", "canciones": [{"titulo": "Pedro Navaja", "artista": "Ruben Blades"}]}

